Subject: [PATCH] Pool framebuffer textures between presets

Creating a new preset's framebuffer textures (glTexImage2D) took 16-58 ms on the
render thread at a preset switch on an NVIDIA SHIELD. Framebuffer attachments of
discarded presets can now go into a per-thread pool and be reused by the next
preset of the same size and format. A reused texture is cleared first, like a new one, so its
old contents never show (only color attachments are pooled).

The pool is off by default; the host enables it with a byte limit
(projectm_opengl_set_texture_pool_limit, 0 empties it) and drops it after a
context loss (projectm_opengl_forget_texture_pool). ProjectM TV only enables it
while enough memory is free.

---
